# Kpix Dashboard — Odoo KPI Module

An Odoo module that provides a board-ready executive KPI dashboard, designed
for shareholders and the board of directors. It turns Odoo's accounting data
into pre-calculated financial indicators, without needing to export reports
manually or wait on heavy live aggregations every time the dashboard loads.

## Description

This module builds a business intelligence layer on top of Odoo's native
accounting models (`account.move.line`, `account.move`, `account.account`),
pre-computing and storing financial KPIs in snapshot records so the dashboard
loads instantly instead of recalculating from the ledger on every page view.

## Key Features

- Pre-calculated KPI snapshots (no live recalculation on page load)
- Revenue, gross margin, EBITDA, net profit, ROE and ROA
- D&A properly isolated from OPEX for accurate EBITDA calculation
- Year-over-year comparisons for all headline KPIs
- Accounts receivable and payable aging in 30-day brackets
- Cash runway estimate based on current burn rate
- Automatic hourly KPI snapshots via a scheduled action
- Configurable EBITDA and runway targets per company (Settings)
- Dedicated read-only Executive/Shareholder security group
- Per-company record-level access via `ir.rule`
- Built on Odoo's standard accounting models — no data duplication or migration

## Requirements

- Odoo 19.0 (Community or Enterprise)
- PostgreSQL 16
- The `account` module installed with data loaded
- No Odoo Enterprise dependency required

## Installation

1. Copy the `shareholder_intelligence_hub` folder into your Odoo instance's
   addons directory (`addons/`, or the path configured in `addons_path`)
2. Restart the Odoo server
3. Enable developer mode and go to **Apps → Update Apps List**
4. Search for "Kpix for Odoo" and install the module

## Local development

This project uses Docker for the development environment. See
`docker-compose.yml` and `odoo.conf` at the project root — they define the
`db` (PostgreSQL 16) and `odoo` (Odoo 19) services, exposed ports
(`8069`, `8072`), and the volume mount for `custom_addons/`.

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

To upgrade the module after a code change to any `.xml`, `.py` or security
file:

```bash
docker compose exec odoo odoo -u shareholder_intelligence_hub -d <your_db_name> \
    --db_host=db --db_user=odoo --db_password=odoo --stop-after-init
docker compose restart odoo
```

